# modbus-scraper's env file — cp env/scraper.env.example env/scraper.env
# and edit. Consumed two ways: `docker run --env-file env/scraper.env
# modbus-scraper` and the compose stack's env_file: (required: false — no
# file = the image defaults). The names are the tool's bare env twins
# (flag > env > the bundled conf > built-in defaults — an env here
# overrides the image's /pv-suite/scraper/scraper.conf knob by knob);
# every line starts commented, the defaults live in the image.

# The upstream cache (HOST:PORT) — the demo default is the stack's
# modbus-cache service (the image's UPSTREAM env).
#UPSTREAM=modbus-cache:15502

# The poll interval in seconds.
#INTERVAL=10

# The prefix of the scraper's own diagnostics metrics (scraper_*); the
# profile/compute metric names carry the profile's prefix (huawei_*).
#METRIC_PREFIX=huawei

# The bearer-token file the exporter serves with. In the compose stack the
# compose's AUTH_TOKEN_FILE (the generated /config/metrics.token) wins —
# environment beats env_file — this line is for plain docker runs. A
# chosen VALUE goes into the file itself, owner-only 0600 (the F12
# discipline).
#AUTH_TOKEN_FILE=/config/metrics.token

# DEBUG|INFO|WARNING|ERROR
#LOG_LEVEL=INFO
